### 5.3 Per-Feature Content Blocks

**Feature A — Hysteresis-Based Self-Healing Recovery**

| Section | Content |
|---|---|
| **Purpose** | Maintain overlay connectivity when a forwarding process or link becomes unavailable, while avoiding route flapping caused by oscillation around a single detection threshold. |
| **Specification — state machine** | Table: `HEALTHY → SUSPECT` (misses ≥ F_thresh, 3); `SUSPECT → FAILED` (misses ≥ N, 5); `FAILED → HEALTHY` (successes ≥ R_thresh, 5); Dead band (R_thresh / F_thresh ≥ 1.5). |
| **Specification — routing & loop protection** | Hop limits, route versioning, next-hop validation, stale-route rejection, unreachable reporting. |
| **Acceptance Criteria** | Recovery with alternate route; no alternate route → unreachable; no persistent loops; sweep `hysteresis_ratio ∈ {1.0 … 3.0}` produces trade-off curve. |
| **Research Anchor** | Maltz thesis (CMU) §7.6.1; two-state hysteresis in VNT control. |

**Feature C — Multipath File Transfer with DB-CMT**

| Section | Content |
|---|---|
| **Purpose** | Transfer a file in chunks across multiple logical overlay paths; reconstruct and verify integrity under heterogeneous conditions. |
| **Specification — scheduler variants** | Table: DB-DSP (min estimated arrival time, primary); Round-Robin (cycle, naïve baseline); Weighted RR (bandwidth-proportional); Single-Path TCP (lowest RTT, lower bound); Naïve Delay-Aware (FD only, ablation). |
| **Specification — retransmission** | RTX-CL: pick path by `cwnd` + loss, not delay alone. Bounded retries; bounded failure on exhaustion. |
| **Acceptance Criteria** | SHA-256 match; interruption recovery; DB-DSP ≤ 50% out-of-order vs RR under 5:1 heterogeneity; RTX-CL ≤ 90% of RTX-CWND transfer time under 5% loss. |
| **Research Anchor** | Verma et al., *J. Network and Systems Management*, 2022; CMT-SCTP literature. |

**Feature D — Linux-Based Network Emulation**

| Section | Content |
|---|---|
| **Purpose** | Reproduce network conditions and serve as the experimental apparatus for Features A and C. |
| **Specification — `tc`/`netem` parameters** | Table: Delay (`delay TIME [JITTER [CORRELATION]]`); Loss (`loss random PERCENT [CORRELATION]`); Duplication; Corruption; Reordering; Rate limit; Queue depth; Seed. |
| **Specification — apparatus** | Fault injection primitives + hysteresis sweep harness for A; path heterogeneity config + scheduler comparison harness for C. |
| **Acceptance Criteria** | Repeatability; documented units/conditions/repetitions/environment; deterministic with fixed seed; config verified and logged per run. |
| **Research Anchor** | Linux `tc-netem(8)`; emulation in TCP BBR / VM research. |

