## 7. Accessibility Checklist

- All feature cards and index rows are `<Link>` or wrapped in `<Link>`; keyboard-accessible by default.
- Feature detail pages set `document.title` to the feature title on mount.
- Prev/Next links have visible focus rings (`outline outline-1 outline-white/40`).
- Sidebar anchors use `<a href="#id">` and scroll the container, not the window.
- Overlay (if enabled) uses `role="dialog" aria-modal="true"`.
- All motion respects `prefers-reduced-motion` — springs collapse to 0-duration fades; mouse-scrub disabled (poster frame shown).
- Contrast: body ≥ `white/45`, labels ≥ `white/40`, large text ≥ `white/30`.
- Videos: `aria-hidden="true"`, `preload="metadata"`, poster fallback for reduced motion and slow networks.

